UPDATE "News"
SET "SlugEn" = 'five-newly-recognized-tourist-attractions-in-lao-cai',
    "ShortTitleEn" = 'Five Newly Recognized Tourist Attractions in Lao Cai',
    "ShortDescriptionEn" = 'Ong Chua Waterfall and the Nhiu Co San, Lao Than, Ky Quan San and Pu Ta Leng peaks in Bat Xat District, Lao Cai, have been recognized as provincial scenic attractions.',
    "ContentBodyEn" = $content$
<p>Specifically, the five scenic attractions in <a href="https://tienphong.vn/tre-co-the-bi-tieu-chay-kiet-ly-nhiem-khuan-duong-ruot-thuong-han-vi-nha-ve-sinh-ban-o-truong-hoc-post1590271.tpo" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(237, 28, 36);">Bat Xat District</a>, <a href="https://tienphong.vn/tag/l%c3%a0o+cai.tpo" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(237, 28, 36);">Lao Cai Province</a>, are Ong Chua Waterfall and Nhiu Co San Peak in Sang Ma Sao Commune; Lao Than Peak in Den Sang, Den Thang and Trinh Tuong communes; and Ky Quan San Peak and Pu Ta Leng Peak in Trung Leng Ho Commune.</p><p><img src="https://cdn.tienphong.vn/images/gUtVM8hm3DVAAYoSYQPpNW-nb9uN1UoZCfCXTofqFr13TGgGnSlw-wfjBi2uojWX2AV8cFVXcuu-kh8mxksiLPVfTUzykeEMODA8XJc7oys/thacongchua-488483-2947.jpg.avif" alt="The majestic beauty of Ong Chua Waterfall. Photo: Lao Cai information portal." height="401" width="708">The majestic beauty of Ong Chua Waterfall. Photo: Lao Cai information portal.</p><p class="ql-align-justify">The chairman of the <a href="https://tienphong.vn/tre-co-the-bi-tieu-chay-kiet-ly-nhiem-khuan-duong-ruot-thuong-han-vi-nha-ve-sinh-ban-o-truong-hoc-post1590271.tpo" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(237, 28, 36);">Lao Cai Provincial People's Committee</a> recently signed a decision recognizing the five locations above as provincial-level <a href="https://tienphong.vn/tag/danh+lam+th%e1%ba%afng+c%e1%ba%a3nh.tpo" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(237, 28, 36);">scenic attractions</a>.</p><p class="ql-align-justify">These destinations possess magnificent, unspoiled beauty, rich ecological landscapes and vegetation, favorable <a href="https://tienphong.vn/dia-oc/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(237, 28, 36);">land</a> and soil conditions, and a cool, fresh climate throughout the year. They retain nearly all of their natural beauty, including streams, waterfalls, diverse flora and extensive primeval forests. These valuable resources offer great potential for developing distinctive forms of ecotourism.</p><p>In addition, the Hmong, Dao and Ha Nhi villages surrounding the protected areas have preserved cultural traditions shaped over a long history. They can support the development of community-based and cultural <a href="https://tienphong.vn/tag/du+l%e1%bb%8bch.tpo" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: rgb(237, 28, 36);">tourism</a>, creating memorable stops along visitors' journeys through these natural landmarks.</p>
$content$
WHERE "NewsId" = '5-diem-du-lich-vua-duoc-cong-nhan-o-lao-cai'
  AND "FlagActive" = TRUE
  AND "ShortTitleEn" = ''
  AND "ShortDescriptionEn" = ''
  AND "ContentBodyEn" = '';

